From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:29:18 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] RetroPlayer: mark the hardware pools before renderers are
 built

"Failed to configure buffer pool", logged every frame with a black screen. The
renderer being configured was a software one, whose ConfigureInternal()
switches on the pixel format and rejects AV_PIX_FMT_NONE - which is exactly what
a hardware stream configures with, since the client renders into a texture we
allocate and there is no format to agree on.

OpenStream() called Configure() and then Create(). Configure() only moves the
render manager to CONFIGURING; the rendering thread then builds renderers from
whichever pools report themselves compatible. Create() is what records the
hardware pools, so running it second lost the race every time.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../RetroPlayer/streams/RetroPlayerRendering.cpp   | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/streams/RetroPlayerRendering.cpp b/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/streams/RetroPlayerRendering.cpp
index 12a34eb..dc48bab 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/streams/RetroPlayerRendering.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/streams/RetroPlayerRendering.cpp
@@ -51,12 +51,24 @@ bool CRetroPlayerRendering::OpenStream(const StreamProperties& properties)
   m_processInfo.SetVideoPixelFormat(pixelFormat);
   m_processInfo.SetVideoDimensions(width, height);
 
+  // Create() before Configure(), not after. Configure() only moves the render
+  // manager to CONFIGURING; the rendering thread then builds renderers from
+  // whichever pools look compatible. Create() is what marks the hardware pools
+  // as the eligible ones, so doing it second loses the race - the software
+  // pool wins, and its ConfigureInternal() rejects AV_PIX_FMT_NONE with
+  // "Failed to configure buffer pool", every frame, forever.
+  //
+  // Safe in this order because the pools themselves are built by CRPProcessInfo
+  // long before either call.
+  if (!m_renderManager.Create(width, height, hwProperties.depth, hwProperties.stencil))
+    return false;
+
   if (!m_renderManager.Configure(pixelFormat, width, height, displayAspectRatio, width, height))
     return false;
 
   CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "RetroPlayer[RENDERING]: Render manager configured");
 
-  return m_renderManager.Create(width, height, hwProperties.depth, hwProperties.stencil);
+  return true;
 }
 
 void CRetroPlayerRendering::CloseStream()
